<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philippe Villiers de L'Isle-Adam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1464–1534</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philippe Villiers de L'Isle-Adam was Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> from 1521. He led the defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> in 1522 and, after its surrender, the Order's years of wandering. In 1530 he accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gozo">Gozo</a> and Tripoli from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> and settled the Order at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birgu">Birgu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippe-villiers-de-lisle-adam.jpg" alt="Philippe Villiers de L'Isle-Adam" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Villiers_de_l_Isle-Adam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
